# broiler-js cldr data pin 1
#
# The Unicode Common Locale Data Repository files the JavaScript profile's Intl tables are generated
# from, and the CLDR licence text. Decision JSD-0027 section 5 asks for CLDR to be pinned by release
# and digest, as JSD-0031 pinned the UCD, and read by nothing but a generator in the architecture test
# project; rule N27 holds the archive and this file to each other, and the generated tables to the
# archive once a generator reads it.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Retrieved twice on 2026-10-04 by Claude into two separate directories; `diff -r`
# over the two found them byte-identical, and every figure below is a reading of the first copy,
# which is the copy archived here. The JSON files are the cldr-json packages cldr-core and
# cldr-bcp47 at 48.2.0 from the npm registry, each tarball checked against the registry's own
# sha512 integrity before it was unpacked; the collation files and the licence are from the CLDR
# repository at the tag release-48-2. The repository owner asked that day for the roadmap's phases
# to be continued, and JSD-0027's recommendation names in-tree generation from pinned CLDR JSON and
# the Unicode License v3 for CLDR on the UCD's terms; no permission specific to this retrieval was
# given, and that is recorded here rather than implied.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. `file <path relative to this directory> <bytes> <sha256>`. A supplemental JSON
# file carries its CLDR version in its `version` object and the generator refuses one that does not
# name the pinned major version; a package.json names the package version; allkeys_CLDR.txt and the
# two CollationTest files name their UCA version in a `# UCA Version:` line; the bcp47 files and the
# three collation XML files carry no version and are held by their hashes alone. The two
# CollationTest files are test-only input: no table is generated from them.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-04 FOR SLICE I2. The number, currency, unit and plural data Intl.NumberFormat reads
# was added the same way: the cldr-json packages cldr-numbers-full and cldr-units-full at 48.2.0, and
# cldr-core again, each tarball checked against the registry's sha512 integrity, retrieved twice into
# two directories and found byte-identical by `cmp` and `diff -r`. From cldr-numbers-full: numbers.json
# for de, en and und, currencies.json for de and en; from cldr-units-full: units.json for de and en;
# from cldr-core: supplemental/currencyData.json, numberingSystems.json, plurals.json and
# pluralRanges.json. The files under main/ carry no version and are held by their hashes alone. The
# cldr-core file archived first is byte-identical in the second tarball. No permission specific to
# this retrieval was given either.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-04 FOR SLICE I3. The date data Intl.DateTimeFormat reads was added the same way: the
# cldr-json package cldr-dates-full at 48.2.0, checked against the registry's sha512 integrity,
# retrieved twice and found byte-identical; from it ca-gregorian.json, dateFields.json and
# timeZoneNames.json for de and en; and from the cldr-core tarball already verified for slice I2,
# supplemental/timeData.json and dayPeriods.json, byte-identical in a third retrieval of that tarball.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-04 FOR SLICE I4. Intl.Locale's week and text information read two more files of the
# cldr-core tarball verified for slice I2, retrieved twice more and found byte-identical to it:
# scriptMetadata.json and supplemental/weekData.json.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-04 FOR SLICE I4, AGAIN. Intl.PluralRules's ordinal rules read one more file of the
# same cldr-core tarball, retrieved twice more, checked against the registry's sha512 integrity and
# found byte-identical to it: supplemental/ordinals.json.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-04 FOR SLICE I4, A THIRD TIME. Intl.ListFormat's patterns come from one more npm
# package, cldr-misc-full at 48.2.0: its tarball, retrieved twice, byte-identical, and checked against
# the registry's sha512 integrity; from it listPatterns.json for de and en and its package.json.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-05 FOR SLICE I4, A FOURTH TIME. Intl.DisplayNames reads one more npm package,
# cldr-localenames-full at 48.2.0, after the repository owner set the Intl data budget to 768 KiB
# that day (JSD-0027 decision (c)): its tarball, retrieved twice, byte-identical, and checked against
# the registry's sha512 integrity; from it languages.json, territories.json, scripts.json,
# variants.json and localeDisplayNames.json for de and en, and its package.json.
#
# EXTENDED 2026-10-05 FOR PHASE F8, SLICE T2. Intl.DateTimeFormat's iso8601 calendar, which the Temporal
# proposal's amendment of ECMA-402 requires among the available calendars, reads its patterns from one
# more file of the CLDR repository at the tag release-48-2, common/main/root.xml: the only locale file
# of the release that defines the iso8601 calendar, whose names it takes from each locale's Gregorian
# calendar. It was retrieved twice on 2026-10-05 and found byte-identical by `cmp`; it carries no
# version and is held by its hash alone. No permission specific to this retrieval was given either.

# EXTENDED 2026-10-05 FOR PHASE F8, SLICE T4. Intl.DateTimeFormat in the calendars the Intl era and
# month code proposal requires reads their names and patterns from eleven more npm packages, the
# cldr-cal-*-full packages at 48.2.0 for the Buddhist, Chinese, Coptic, Dangi, Ethiopic, Hebrew, Indian,
# Islamic, Japanese, Persian and ROC calendars: each tarball retrieved twice on 2026-10-05, found
# byte-identical by `cmp`, and checked against the registry's sha512 integrity; from each its
# package.json and its ca-*.json files for de and en, but ca-islamic-rgsa.json, a calendar Temporal
# refuses. From the cldr-dates-full tarball verified for slice I3, retrieved twice more and found
# byte-identical to it, ca-generic.json for de and en, whose patterns the calendars without their own
# inherit. The repository owner asked that day for slice T4 to be continued; no permission specific
# to this retrieval was given either.

